From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:19:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i386-asm: VEX and EVEX encodings (AVX, AVX2, BMI1/2,
 AVX-512VL subset)

The Linux kernel's lib/crypto/x86 SHA-1, SHA-256, BLAKE2s and POLYVAL
files (sha1-ssse3-and-avx.S, sha1-avx2-asm.S, sha256-avx-asm.S,
sha256-avx2-asm.S, polyval-pclmul-avx.S, blake2s-core.S) are VEX-encoded
AVX and AVX2 code with BMI2's rorx and andn, and the BLAKE2s AVX-512
function uses vprord, vpternlogd and vpermi2d with xmm/ymm operands
(EVEX, AVX-512VL).

* %ymm0-15 as a register class (OP_YMM; OPT_VEC in a template takes an
  xmm or a ymm register and VEX.L follows the operand), four operands
  per instruction (MAX_OPERANDS 4, DEF_ASM_OP4).
* Table flags OPC_VEX / OPC_EVEX: the entry's 0x66/0xf3/0xf2 high byte
  is the pp field, OPC_0F/OPC_0F38/OPC_0F3A the map, a 64-bit register
  operand or OPC_48/OPC_VEXW the W bit.  asm_vex_prefix() writes the
  2-byte C5 form when it suffices, else C4, or the 4-byte EVEX prefix
  (no masking, broadcast or rounding; disp8*N for its memory operands).
  No REX and no operand-size prefix for these entries.
* Operand roles in AT&T order: ModRM.r/m is the template's
  memory-capable operand, ModRM.reg the last register operand (the
  destination), VEX.vvvv the register operand left (the first source);
  OPC_NDD for the shift-by-immediate forms, where the destination is
  vvvv and ModRM.reg the group.
* 32-bit code uses the same encoder with registers 0-7; ymm8-15 and the
  64-bit forms of the general-register instructions need 64-bit code.

Entries: vzeroupper/vzeroall; the moves (vmovdqa/u, vmovaps/ups,
vmovapd/upd, vmovntdq/a, vmovd/q, vmovhlps/lhps); broadcasts and the
sign/zero extensions; the packed integer arithmetic, logic, compares,
unpacks, packs, multiplies and the SSSE3/SSE4.1 additions as vp*; the
floating-point logic, arithmetic and unpacks; vptest, vpabs*, vpermd/ps;
the shifts by xmm/m128 and by imm8; vpshufd/hw/lw, vpermq/pd,
vshufps/pd, vpalignr, vpblendw/d, vperm2i128/f128, vinserti128/f128,
vextracti128/f128; vpclmulqdq and vaes* in their 128-bit forms;
vpinsr*/vpextr*; BMI1/2: andn, blsr, blsmsk, blsi, bzhi, sarx, shlx,
shrx, pdep, pext, mulx, rorx; EVEX: vprord/l, vprorq/l, vpternlogd/q,
vpermi2d/q, vpermt2d/q.  Encodings byte-compared with GNU as in 32- and
64-bit mode (about 400 forms).
---
 i386-asm.c   | 204 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 i386-tok.h   |  19 ++++
 x86_64-asm.h | 246 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 431 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

